From: Wittmoon <jmoon@lunarink.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:11:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 30/35] placement_edits: score several candidate traces per
 cell against the human's pick

--candidate NAME=TIFXYZ (repeatable, same grid as --before) adds per worst
cell the distance from the edited surface to each candidate, each
candidate's own CT-peak offset with --volume, `chosen` (the candidate the
human ended nearest to) and `audit_pick` (the candidate the audit would rank
best). Candidate points go in edits.npz, names in provenance.json. The
audit stays a single measurement; this is how several tracers get compared
against the human's final call. Test with on-sheet and off-sheet candidates.
---
