Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:31:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] placement_edits: rank candidates on absolute offset,
 measure unflagged cells, cube level

Review fixes. audit_pick ranked on |median signed offset|, so a candidate
+4 on one side of a cell and -4 on the other scored 0; it now ranks on the
median absolute offset (aoff_<name>) and records nvalid_<name>, and a
candidate with usable points on fewer than a quarter of the cell (or
fewer than 10) abstains. --all-cells marked every cell outside the capped
worst-cells list as unflagged with a blank offset, which read as on-sheet;
with --volume those cells now get their own measured median_offset and
n_valid, and the docs say what unflagged means. ct_cube ignored --level
and assumed a 3-D volume. The audit wrote <name>.json before
n_worst_cells was set, so the JSON and aggregate.csv disagreed. Three
tests.
---
 vesuvius/docs/surface-placement-audit.md      |  7 +-
 .../image_proc/run/surface_placement_audit.py |  4 +-
 .../src/vesuvius/scripts/placement_edits.py   | 89 +++++++++++++------
 vesuvius/tests/test_placement_edits.py        | 41 +++++++++
 4 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

