From c8db970e1c4e59e974e7b9e498c3635554c4ce0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wittmoon <jmoon@lunarink.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:31:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 33/35] review_disagreements: rank model-vs-label disagreement,
 stage blind tiles, export corrected labels

Adds vesuvius/scripts/review_disagreements.py, the model-side counterpart
of review_holes.py. Given a label folder and a folder of surface
predictions it ranks crops by the fraction of predicted papyrus more than
--tol voxels from any labelled papyrus (ignore value excluded), keeps
connected far components of at least --min-vox voxels, and writes
queue.csv and candidates.csv. --stage-only renders one blind tile per
candidate (z/y/x slices, label and model outlines, marker on the model
sheet) with a sheet.csv for the reader and a separate key.csv, so the
reader never sees the crop id or rank. The marker is the component voxel
nearest its centroid, not the centroid itself, so it cannot land off a
concave component. The terminal review is resumable and keyed by
crop+marker; --export-training writes examples in the trainer layout
(images/<id>.tif, labels/<id>_<target>.tif): the marker's component is
set for "sheet", the label is left unchanged for "not", "unclear" is
skipped. Restaging refuses to overwrite a sheet.csv that already holds
verdicts.

review_holes.py: the trainer-layout writer is extracted into
write_trainer_pair() so both scripts share it; no behaviour change.

Tests: vesuvius/tests/test_review_disagreements.py (8) plus the existing
review_holes tests, 12 passed.
