Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:17:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 34/35] review_disagreements: rank-stratified staging with
 blind decoy tiles

A reader who only sees candidates cannot show they say NOT when NOT is right, and ten tiles from the top of the queue say nothing about how deep it stays real. Add --ranks (stage --limit crops from each queue position), --decoys N (control points per candidate, alternating label-and-model-covered and off-sheet, shuffled into the S-series with --seed, no outlines in a decoy sitting), kind and rank in key.csv, a per-kind/per-rank verdict tally printed after a review, and exclusion of decoys from --export-training. Three tests.
---
 .../vesuvius/scripts/review_disagreements.py  | 121 ++++++++++++++----
 vesuvius/tests/test_review_disagreements.py   |  48 +++++++
 2 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

